    "save_id": "food:baigana-poda",
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "taste",
        "title": "The transformation beneath the skin",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "Begin with the contrast: the darkened outside, the yielding flesh within. The finished bowl tells only half the story; ask the cook about the moment before the peeling.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          },
          {
            "text": "In Sasmita’s baigana poda recipe, eggplant is roasted over a gas flame, peeled and mashed with mustard oil and aromatics.",
            "source_ids": [
              "food-baigana-sasmita2020"
            ],
            "kind": "sourced_summary"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "making",
        "title": "One recipe, room for another",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "This is one cook’s documented preparation. The photograph shows a combined eggplant-and-tomato dish, baigana-bilati poda; it should not be read as a photograph of her eggplant-only recipe.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          },
          {
            "text": "A useful kitchen question is wonderfully simple: do you roast the vegetables separately, or bring them together at the end? Let the maker describe their own version.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "meal",
        "title": "Make space beside the pakhala",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "Sasmita presents the dish as an accompaniment to pakhala. The connection offers a way to explore a meal through its smaller bowls.",
            "source_ids": [
              "food-baigana-sasmita2020"
            ],
            "kind": "sourced_summary"
          },
          {
            "text": "Read the pakhala and Badi chura stories alongside this one. Build a tasting wish list, then ask what is available together on the day. There is no fixed menu to complete.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "try",
        "title": "Take a question to the cook",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "Ask what is mixed into the mash, how much chilli is used, and whether mustard oil, onion or garlic is included. Mention any ingredients you avoid.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          },
          {
            "text": "No outlet or cooking demonstration is verified here. A named maker, a place and permission to share their account would help this story grow.",
            "source_ids": [],
            "kind": "editorial_invitation"
          }
        ]
